+---
+name: upload-to-gdrive
+description: Automatically convert and upload generated readable documents to Google Drive. Use this whenever you generate a long readable document (like an analysis, story, plan, or research report) that the user might want to read away from the computer.
+---
+
+# Instructions
+
+When you generate a readable document for the user, you MUST automatically upload a copy to their Google Drive as a `.docx` file. 
+
+To do this, you must run the `md_to_gdrive.py` script provided in this skill's `scripts/` directory.
+
+### Command Format
+```bash
+python "<absolute_path_to_this_skill_directory>\scripts\md_to_gdrive.py" "<absolute_path_to_markdown_file>" "[optional_document_title]"
+```
+
+* `<absolute_path_to_markdown_file>`: The path to the generated document artifact (e.g. `C:\Users\spurd\.gemini\antigravity\brain\...\my_document.md`).
+* `[optional_document_title]`: (Optional) The name you want the `.docx` file to have in Google Drive. If omitted, it will use the original markdown file's basename.
+
+### Example
+```bash
+python "<absolute_path_to_this_skill_directory>\scripts\md_to_gdrive.py" "C:\Users\spurd\.gemini\antigravity\brain\12345\analysis.md" "Analysis Report"
+```
